      \field{sortinit}{G}
      \field{sortinithash}{32d67eca0634bf53703493fb1090a2e8}
      \field{labelnamesource}{author}
      \field{labeltitlesource}{title}
      \field{abstract}{DNN accelerators are often developed and evaluated in isolation without considering the cross-stack, system-level effects in real-world environments. This makes it difficult to appreciate the impact of System-on-Chip (SoC) resource contention, OS overheads, and programming-stack inefficiencies on overall performance/energy-efficiency. To address this challenge, we present Gemmini, an open-source1, full-stack DNN accelerator generator. Gemmini generates a wide design-space of efficient ASIC accelerators from a flexible architectural template, together with flexible programming stacks and full SoCs with shared resources that capture system-level effects. Gemmini-generated accelerators have also been fabricated, delivering up to three orders-of-magnitude speedups over high-performance CPUs on various DNN benchmarks.}
      \field{booktitle}{Proceedings of the 58th Annual ACM/IEEE Design Automation Conference}
      \field{isbn}{9781665432740}
      \field{title}{Gemmini: Enabling Systematic Deep-Learning Architecture Evaluation via Full-Stack Integration}
      \field{year}{2022}
